        "headingId": 471,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lung</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T15:30:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 709,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 472,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 108500,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 432,
        "headingId": 472,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FLIT manifests in the first 3&nbsp;months of life as a solid or microcystic lung mass {21107081}. Most infants present with respiratory difficulties. Imaging studies show well-circumscribed solid or partially cystic masses. Some cases are detectable by prenatal ultrasound. One prenatally diagnosed infant presented with hydrops {21683234}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T15:30:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 710,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 473,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 108501,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 432,
        "headingId": 473,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Insufficient data</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T15:30:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 711,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 474,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 108502,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 432,
        "headingId": 474,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T15:30:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 712,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 475,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 108503,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 432,
        "headingId": 475,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The pathogenesis is unknown. A subset of cases are associated with <em>ALK</em> gene fusions {24965693; 28705706}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T15:30:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 719,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 482,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 108504,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 432,
        "headingId": 482,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FLIT appears as well-circumscribed, intraparenchymal, solid or spongy microcystic masses ranging from 20&nbsp;to 70&nbsp;mm in size.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T15:30:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 713,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 476,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 108505,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 432,
        "headingId": 476,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FLIT consists of immature-appearing airspaces with widened septa containing uniform, bland, evenly spaced mesenchymal cells {21107081}. These cells have round to ovoid nuclei with dispersed chromatin and a rim of clear or pale-pink cytoplasm and well-defined cell borders. Airway spaces are lined by flattened or cuboidal epithelium with clear cytoplasm. Some cases show areas of fibroblastic or myofibroblastic cells that expand the septa and overgrow the airspaces. These areas may have scattered inflammatory cells including plasma cells and resemble inflammatory myofibroblastic tumour. It is notable that foci resembling inflammatory myofibroblastic tumour appear to arise as the patient (tumour) ages {21107081; 28705706}. The tumour is well demarcated from normal lung with or without a thin fibrous capsule. Tumour cells show positivity for vimentin with variable staining for SMA and desmin. Both the interstitial mesenchymal cells and the lining cells contain abundant glycogen. FLIT resembles type&nbsp;I pleuropulmonary blastoma in that it shows proliferation of interstitial mesenchymal cells and arises in early infancy. FLIT tumour cells are more uniformly distributed in the septa and have smaller airspaces than those in type&nbsp;I pleuropulmonary blastoma. Cytologically, FLIT cells lack nuclear hyperchromatism and mitotic activity and have better-defined cytoplasm than type&nbsp;I pleuropulmonary blastoma cells.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T15:30:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 714,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 477,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 108506,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 432,
        "headingId": 477,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T15:30:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 715,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 478,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 108507,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 432,
        "headingId": 478,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Some cases of FLIT have shown <em>ALK</em> fusions, specifically <em>A2M</em>::<em>ALK</em> {24965693; 28705706}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T15:30:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 718,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 481,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 108508,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 432,
        "headingId": 481,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a well-circumscribed, solid or spongy lung mass in an infant; histology shows widened alveolar septa containing bland, uniform mesenchymal cells.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-10T15:30:49"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
